From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 07:36:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] base-files: fwtool: read the firmware keys from
 /etc/usign/keys

The keys that sign firmware images are usign keys, which ucert checks
an image's signature against. fwtool_check_signature() read them from
/etc/opkg/keys, opkg's directory, which images built with apk no longer
need for anything else.

Read them from /etc/usign/keys, named after the tool whose keys they
are as /etc/apk/keys is, and from /etc/opkg/keys on an image that has no
such directory, so that every image keeps checking its signatures as
before.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/base-files/files/lib/upgrade/fwtool.sh | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/package/base-files/files/lib/upgrade/fwtool.sh b/package/base-files/files/lib/upgrade/fwtool.sh
index 0bc6e69..eaee053 100644
--- a/package/base-files/files/lib/upgrade/fwtool.sh
+++ b/package/base-files/files/lib/upgrade/fwtool.sh
@@ -18,8 +18,12 @@ fwtool_check_signature() {
 		return 0
 	fi
 
+	# The firmware keys: usign's, or opkg's directory on an image without it.
+	local keys=/etc/usign/keys
+	[ -d "$keys" ] || keys=/etc/opkg/keys
+
 	fwtool -q -T -s /dev/null "$1" | \
-		ucert -V -m - -c "/tmp/sysupgrade.ucert" -P /etc/opkg/keys
+		ucert -V -m - -c "/tmp/sysupgrade.ucert" -P "$keys"
 
 	return $?
 }
